# Local-only debug artifacts - device coredumps/logs can contain WiFi/device
# details and must never be committed; never commit these. The two `debug*`
# patterns cover both this project's own download naming and a browser's
# "(1)" duplicate-download suffix (found live: a real `debug (1).log` sat
# untracked in a battery-analysis scratch folder below, matched by neither
# the old pattern nor any other rule here).
photoframe-debug*.log*
debug*.log*
CoreDUMP*.7z
_BuildCMD.txt
# Found live: a user-created battery-analysis scratch folder holding a
# downloaded debug log, battery-history export, and system-info export -
# same "device debug artifact" category as the log patterns above (a MAC
# address alone in system-info.json's device_id, plus whatever the log
# contains), just under a folder name the log/coredump patterns don't reach.
_BATT_ANAL/

# Local-only audit/working notes - not meant for the repo history.
docs/AGENDA_AUDIT.md
docs/FIRMWARE_AUDIT.md
docs/examples/

# Local editor/tool configs - not project-wide settings
.claude/
.vscode/
bmp_overlay_plan.txt
coredump_report.txt
